      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Nifedipine-induced gingival hyperplasia was first reported in 1984. Nifedipine is a relatively new drug used in the treatment of ventricular arrhythmias and angina. This article reports a case of gingival hyperplasia induced by the drug and reviews the cases reported so far in the literature."},
